From d51db13f7dbd5602ec746cc0b3cacb1c87a46abc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: onlyfish <linotfish@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:09:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Settings: add a game mode screen

Apps -> Game mode lists the installed apps. Tapping an entry opens a per
game screen with the app name on top, the game mode selector, one toggle
per behaviour and a save / back bar at the bottom:

  Game mode             Standard / Performance / Battery, handed to the
                        system game manager
  Notification banners  do not pop up while this game is running
  Mute notifications    no sound and no vibration
  ANGLE renderer        pin the game to the ANGLE GL driver

Nothing is written until the user hits save, so backing out leaves the
game untouched. Saving marks the package as a game; long pressing an
entry in the list removes it again. The list and the flags live in
Settings.Secure, so they can also be maintained with adb.

Two things the layout has to work around: the activity theme inherits
from Theme.DeviceDefault.Settings, so every Material widget needs its own
android:theme, and ?attr/materialButtonOutlinedStyle must be avoided
because themes_bridge points it at a Material 2 style whose textAppearance
the platform theme lacks. The segmented selector therefore reuses the
styles SegmentedButtonPreference already ships.

BaseAppListSettingsFragment gains hooks to navigate on tap and refresh on
resume instead of toggling the entry, and its selection bookkeeping is
keyed by package name rather than list position, which shifted as soon as
the list was re-sorted.

Change-Id: Ibe4914b1a566f0d5278ac82f60e6246aa745a95b
